# Review test for M7's failure path (user/root/src/release_fault.rs;
# docs/design.md, "Failures"): on the kernel built without features, the
# root task revokes its COM1 IOPort, deleting uart's copy, while it waits
# in console's Write and console in uart's. uart's port access fails, its
# panic message's DebugPutChar raises UnknownSyscall, the kernel sends the
# fault to endpoint F, and watch writes TEST FAIL through Polled on the
# root task's COM1 IOPort and ends the run through isa-debug-exit with
# failure. Nothing else reports it: the kernel prints nothing.
kernel: release
cmdline: test=release_fault
exit: failure
expect: loader: microL4 loader
expect: release_fault: revoking the COM1 IOPort, which deletes uart's copy
expect: TEST FAIL: uart fault 2 (UnknownSyscall), MR0 to MR3
forbid: console answered after uart lost its IOPort
forbid: watch did not end the run
forbid: microL4 kernel
forbid: DEBUG HALT
forbid: KERNEL PANIC
